###############################################################################
# CSV import fixtures - byte-exact test data, never normalised.
#
# The repository root normalises everything git detects as text to LF. These
# files must not be: the CRLF line endings are what Swiss bank exports actually
# use and are part of what the reader is tested against, Latin1.csv is Latin-1
# rather than UTF-8 on purpose, and Utf8Bom.csv carries a byte-order mark.
# Normalising any of that would quietly disarm the tests that exist to catch a
# decoder or a line-ending assumption going wrong.
###############################################################################
*.csv -text
